  speakerName: Sally
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  dialogueText: 'Sometimes you want to ask for help more politely.

    In Ilokano,
    ''mabalin kadi a tulunganak?'' means ''can you help me?''

    This is useful
    when politely requesting someone''s assistance.

    Listen carefully: mabalin
    kadi a tulunganak?

    Now, try saying ''mabalin kadi a tulunganak?'' yourself.'
